# How every shipped SVG under parts/bell is drawn. Checked by
# lasermade-tools' repro-svg; $OUT is where the file must be written.
#
# NOTHING RAN THESE GENERATORS AT ALL until 2026-09-10. The block bores had two
# byte gates and the ribbon sheets a third; knotwork-soundholes and living-hinge
# grew one each when it turned out four of their knots recorded their command
# nowhere. The bell and the mouthpiece -- eleven generators between them -- were
# watched by none of it, and the one thing that did touch this directory, the
# previews gate, checks the preview against the cut file rather than the cut
# file against the code. So the sheet on disk could be one the current code
# would no longer draw, and every gate would still have been green.
#
# It also matters more here than elsewhere: these generators WRITE when you run
# them. A stray argument used to be dropped in silence and the defaults drawn,
# so `bell.rs --help` wrote eight sheets rather than printing anything. They
# refuse a valueless switch now, and this manifest is what says the sheets they
# do write are the ones that shipped.

cut-files/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86-cut-files.svg :: ../../target/release/bell-round 17 --bore=10 --length=152 --mouth=80 --out=$OUT

# The two display drawings. Both are read back OUT of the cut file above rather
# than recomputed, so they cannot describe a bell the sheet does not cut.
bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86-section.svg :: ../../target/release/bell-section cut-files/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86-cut-files.svg $OUT
bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86-view.svg :: ../../target/release/bell-view cut-files/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86-cut-files.svg $OUT

# The preview. all-gates.sh walks every previews/ directory and checks this one
# too; it is claimed here as well so that nothing under this directory is
# unaccounted for, which is the whole point of the manifest. The tool lives in
# the sibling lasermade-tools checkout, hence the climb.
previews/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86-cut-files.svg :: ../../../lasermade-tools/target/release/make-preview cut-files/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86-cut-files.svg $OUT

# The turn page: the same rings as a solid you can rotate. It is a shipped
# artefact that no gate reached until .repro learned to walk *.html -- doc-audit
# pairs a page with a markdown document of the same name, and this one has no
# markdown at all, so it sat outside every check there was.
bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86-turn.html :: ../../target/release/part-view cut-files/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86-cut-files.svg $OUT

# The port-to-bell adapter, added 2026-09-13. It carries the 7 x 14mm port of a
# swept-curve bore into the 10mm round throat this bell starts at, over seven
# rings and 21mm, holding area across the change rather than diameter. It was
# unclaimed here for the three days it existed, which is exactly the hole the
# header above describes: a generator nothing ran, shipping a sheet nothing
# compared. repro-svg reported it as UNCLAIMED and that is how it was found.
cut-files/bell-adapter-port7x14-to-bore10-7rings-x1-cut-files.svg :: ../../target/release/bell-adapter --out=$OUT
previews/bell-adapter-port7x14-to-bore10-7rings-x1-cut-files.svg :: ../../../lasermade-tools/target/release/make-preview cut-files/bell-adapter-port7x14-to-bore10-7rings-x1-cut-files.svg $OUT

# The SolidCraft design (2026-11-08): its script, the design (slimmed by
# sc-slim so it is the same every run), and the STEP file SolidCraft builds
solidcraft/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86.solidcraft.json :: ../../target/release/bell-round 17 --bore=10 --length=152 --mouth=80 --solidcraft=$(dirname $OUT)/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86.solidcraft.json
solidcraft/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86.sc :: ../../target/release/bell-round 17 --bore=10 --length=152 --mouth=80 --solidcraft=$(dirname $OUT)/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86.solidcraft.json >/dev/null && solidcraft-cli run $(dirname $OUT)/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86.solidcraft.json --save $OUT --quiet && ../../../lasermade-tools/target/release/sc-slim $OUT
step/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86.step :: ../../target/release/bell-round 17 --bore=10 --length=152 --mouth=80 --solidcraft=$(dirname $OUT)/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86.solidcraft.json >/dev/null && solidcraft-cli run $(dirname $OUT)/bell-round10-153mm-17rings-x3-rim86.solidcraft.json --out $OUT --quiet
